# UX: adoption, process, product-carrier, effect and closure meanings stay distinct.
L(U,'ux-method','UX Method member title and profile-binding marker; scope is decided by adoption/default/exemption owners.')
C(U,'governing-relations','On covered UX surfaces, typed input, command dispatch, replay and closure bind exact Product contracts, algebras, current owning state, evidence and actual effect/decision grants.','Each typed-input, dispatch, replay or closure consumer within adopted/default-covered UX scope.','ux_contract','UX owns TEA realization, local ephemera rule, typed effect membrane, runtime validation, replay/accessibility and bounded escrow; project design owns stack/exemptions.',ob='Apply Contract application with local fields once at each consumer.||Conjoin applicable Design and UX closure obligations; command emission grants neither Product-truth nor continuation authority.||Keep ODD execution and World Model semantics conditional on their separate selection.',deps=T+'contract-application|contract_application '+F+'result-conjunction|result_contract',ins='adoption algebras owning_state product_contract effects replay design',extra={'contract_bindings':[{'contract':T+'contract-application','local_subjects':['typed input into UX State','Cmd dispatch to admitted Product carrier','interaction-family replay','UX closure'],'required_relations':['shared typed Product contract','current runtime-owned State','declared Msg/Update/Cmd/Sub cases','actual operation/decision mandate','evidence and admitted effect cases'],'result_boundaries':['input admissibility','Product operation outcome','replay correctness','UX method closure remain separate']} ]})
D(U,'1-position','Adopted UX uses TEA: runtime-owned typed State, pure View and Update, typed Msg transitions and Cmd-valued effects interpreted at a declared membrane; View owns no continuation.','Interpreting the adopted UX process model.','ux_state','TEA is an additional domain policy, not a consequence of finite capacity alone.',ob='No product-meaningful view mutation, two-way binding without Msg or effect handlers as controllers.',perm='The §5 bounded ephemera exception retains its exact unmount/visibility conditions.',deps=U+'5-state-transition-law '+U+'6-effect-membrane-rule',ins='adoption algebras owning_state')
C(U,'1a-constitutional-authority-rule','After Product/ticket/design/review adoption, UX Method is sole realization authority on that surface; local ADRs select stack but cannot weaken its process model.','Determining authority for an adopted UX surface.','ux_adoption','Evidence from existing code, convention, screenshots, comments, history, prototypes or generated artifacts does not override method.',ob='Ambiguity fails closed before implementation: satisfy stricter reading, reprice through constitutional method or record scoped design exemption.',perm='Stack choice remains local under preservation; a valid scoped exemption changes only its named applicability.',deps=U+'13-adoption-guidance '+U+'13a-scaffold-and-exemption-law',ins='adoption design')
D(U,'2-method-role','Spec owns constitutional process/re-entry, ODD graph-native carriers, Design deterministic module realization; UX adds TEA render/lifecycle/browser/layout/accessibility discipline on covered UX modules.','Selecting owners for UX module realization.','ux_contract','Shared immutability/totality/effect-edge/no-semantic-center/coupling remain Design-owned; UX refines without duplicating authority.',ins='adoption design')
D(U,'3-method-composition','UX modules combine applicable Design and UX disciplines; non-UX modules need only Design. Selected ODD projection/query surfaces that include UX add UX realization without moving graph ownership.','Classifying a module or ODD projection/query surface.','ux_adoption','Composition is per surface; method availability does not impose UX on non-UX modules.',deps=U+'2-method-role',ins='adoption design')
C(U,'3a-ux-projection-and-constructive-carrier-boundary','Each product-truth-changing Msg maps to an admitted Product carrier; View only projects admitted truth and emits typed control messages.','A message can affect assets, Context/selection/pins/global state, sessions/work dispatch, closure/approval/continuation/lineage/provenance/evidence or publication/disposition.','ux_contract','Allowed carriers: AssetSurface action, published graph function/composition, design-admitted workorder/job/runtime command, ABG event/command where ABG owns runtime, or another named typed Product contract.',ob='Missing admitted carrier blocks the truth-changing action until carrier authored or requirement repriced.||UX may not become hidden constructive owner.',perm='Expansion, sorting, filter text, focus and drafts may use UX-local Msg under local-state bounds.',deps=U+'7-assetsurface-binding-rule '+U+'5-state-transition-law',ins='product_contract algebras owning_state')
D(U,'4-process-model--elm-architecture','State is runtime-held; Msg enumerates typed user/system actions; pure Update:(Msg,State)->(State,Cmd) describes effects; pure View:State->ViewTree projects State; runtime interprets typed Cmd/Sub and owns the loop.','Realizing a covered UX surface.','ux_state','The runtime renders, receives Msg, reduces State/Cmd and interprets effects; process shape is mandatory within adoption.',ob='Same input State yields same View; Update schedules effects without performing them.',ins='algebras owning_state effects')
D(U,'4a-process-model-without-language-or-framework-mandate','Project chooses stack in its design and demonstrates preservation of TEA §§4–8; no language/framework ranking follows from this method.','Choosing or reviewing a UX implementation stack.','ux_adoption','Language-integrated runtime, explicit reducer/interpreter, signals behind reducer and server-side request/response realization are non-normative possibilities.',ob='Reject view-owned continuation, render effects, product state mutation outside reducer and hidden multi-step view state; reject no-Msg two-way binding, imperative render DOM and controller effect handlers.||Record framework and short preservation justification.',deps=U+'4-process-model--elm-architecture '+U+'5-state-transition-law '+U+'6-effect-membrane-rule '+U+'8-ux-twin-of-odd-115a--view-does-not-own-continuation',ins='design algebras effects')
C(U,'5-state-transition-law','Product-meaningful State changes only through typed Msg and pure Update; local cells are permitted only when their loss on unmount changes neither Product behavior nor another UI view.','Declaring or implementing State transitions and local state.','ux_state','Runtime algebras and the unmount test distinguish canonical state from ephemera.',ob='Declare State, Msg, Update, Cmd and Sub when subscribed.||Each Cmd names effect kind, typed payload, admitted target, exhaustive observed/unresolved outcome Msg cases with reason/observation, and needed deterministic correlation.||Update performs no I/O, side-channel logging or global mutation.',perm='Open/closed, hover and drafts may use local cells only if unobserved by other views, outside Product state and inconsequential after unmount.||Product-meaningful state has no ephemera exception.',deps=U+'4-process-model--elm-architecture '+U+'6-effect-membrane-rule',ins='algebras owning_state product_contract effects',extra={'state_classifier':{'local_ephemera_if':'not observed by other views AND not part of Product state AND no Product/UI consequence on unmount','reducer_required_if':'losing value changes Product behavior OR another UI view','unknown':'unknown visibility/unmount consequence cannot justify the ephemera exception'}})
C(U,'6-effect-membrane-rule','Declared Cmd interpretation confines effects to the membrane and returns typed reason-bearing observations; business transitions remain in Update and uncertain dispatch is reconciled against current owning state before dependent repetition.','Interpreting UX Cmd/Sub or recovering after uncertain effect outcomes.','ux_effect','Membrane interprets one declared Cmd per effect; platform handler name alone does not make a handler lawful.',ob='I/O, subscriptions and imperative platform interop only in the membrane, never render/pure helper/Update.||Reducer owns branching, state derivation and multi-step business decisions.||Relate every qualified outcome Msg to its effect observation boundary/evidence, including applicable non-start/reversal, partial/unknown and missing-reason cases.||A failed transport return after dispatch may mean unknown mutation; declared recovery observes actual owner before dependent repeat.',perm='Host DOM/filesystem/native interop and external subscription are allowed at declared membrane.||Old success messages or reconstructed UI context cannot override current owning observation.',deps=F+'workspace-and-context|recovery_contract '+F+'result-algebra|effect_observation_contract '+U+'5-state-transition-law',ins='algebras effects owning_state product_contract',mapping={'contract_ref':'core_result','local_predicate':'Cmd/outcome binding preserves Product authority and actual observed effect state','domain_mapping':'Each typed Msg plus cause/evidence maps onto its declared observation boundary; message name alone never determines effect or verdict. Missing reason remains indeterminate support.','effect_cases':['not_requested','not_started','completed','partial','reverted','unknown'],'unknown':'lost response after possible mutation remains unknown; preserve observed parts and recover actual owner before dependent repeat','non_equivalences':['dispatch != completion','failed response != not_started','reconstructed State != current owner','membrane interpretation != business continuation']},extra={'contract_bindings':[{'contract':F+'workspace-and-context','local_subject':'actual Product state affected by uncertain Cmd','required_before':'dependent repeat','evidence':'declared recovery Cmd current owning-state observation; established subject-specific idempotence required for any idempotence reliance','forbidden_inference':'failed response or empty UI log establishes no effect'}]})
C(U,'7-assetsurface-binding-rule','UX State derives from shared AssetSurface projections and truth-changing Msg maps one-to-one to registry actions or a documented semantics-preserving projection; writes and selection use the admitted Product contracts.','Binding a UX surface to Product truth/actions.','ux_contract','If AssetSurface is absent, design must name an equivalent typed contract and preserve the same binding law.',ob='Do not redeclare asset shape locally.||Selection emits Context/equivalent consistent with Product selection contract.||Writes use action registry/equivalent, not direct file/service calls.||No admitted contract blocks truth-changing UX actions.',perm='UX-local actions remain only local concerns; faithful explicit action projection may wrap registry entries.',deps=U+'3a-ux-projection-and-constructive-carrier-boundary '+U+'10-type-sharing-rule',ins='product_contract algebras owning_state')
C(U,'8-ux-twin-of-odd-115a--view-does-not-own-continuation','Runtime/reducer owns state continuation; every product-meaningful phase transition is an explicit Msg over State and replayable without hidden view memory.','Covered UX state continuation or multi-step interaction.','ux_state','This is the UX analogue of selected ODD/ABG continuation ownership, not an unconditional ABG requirement.',ob='No view-determined next state, unmessaged local chains or hidden inter-event refs/closures/module variables.||Move multi-step state machine into State and reducer; view projects current phase.',perm='Strictly bounded §5 view-local ephemera retain their exception.',deps=U+'5-state-transition-law '+U+'8a-msg-replay-proof-requirement',ins='algebras owning_state replay')
C(U,'8a-msg-replay-proof-requirement','For each product-meaningful interaction family, executable replay produces expected final State, ordered Cmds and typed returns from its declared initial fixture, ordered Msg log and injected deterministic inputs.','Before claiming UX method closure for every covered Product UX surface.','ux_replay','Replay correctness and actual effect completion are separate predicates.',ob='Retain initial fixture, ordered log, final State, ordered Cmds, typed return Msgs including admitted unresolved effects, injected time/randomness/IDs/external payloads.||Reject correctness depending on undeclared DOM state, refs/module variables/closures/timers/effect-handler memory, external results bypassing Msg, or unmount-persistent Product consequences in view-local state.||Conjoin all required interaction families and applicable closure checks, retaining failed families and missing coverage.',perm='A projection-only contract may have a no-effect proof with empty Cmd sequence.||Correct reproduction of an unknown-effect Msg may satisfy replay while effect completion stays unknown.',deps=F+'result-conjunction|result_contract '+U+'5-state-transition-law '+U+'6-effect-membrane-rule',ins='algebras replay effects',mapping={'contract_ref':'core_result','local_predicate':'exact interaction-family replay State/Cmd/typed-return expectations hold under declared conditions','satisfied':'performed replay establishes expected State, ordered Cmd/returns and admitted deterministic inputs','falsified':'expected-state/command mismatch or demonstrated dependency on excluded state/input','indeterminate':'missing decisive trace; not-run proof retains not_performed and cannot satisfy','invalid_basis':'unusable fixture/governing basis','out_of_frame':'interaction outside assessment domain','effects':'expected unknown-effect output does not establish underlying completion','empty_commands':'valid no-effect evidence only if that interaction contract declares no effect'})
C(U,'9-view-shape-rule','View consumes declared typed inputs and returns typed ViewTree purely, without hidden mutable capture or undeclared reads across renders.','Rendering a covered UX surface.','ux_state','Function/component/template/server handler/signal syntax is a local stack choice; State->ViewTree purity governs.',ob='Declare all consumed state/props/context; no side effects in render body.||Out-of-render mutable refs read in render violate rule unless covered by the explicit declared platform-handle effect-membrane exception.',perm='A design-named platform handle for imperative interop at the membrane is the stated exception; it does not permit hidden Product state.',deps=U+'6-effect-membrane-rule '+U+'5-state-transition-law',ins='algebras design effects')
C(U,'10-type-sharing-rule','UX imports Product record types from the shared contract; every untrusted/out-of-process seam validates at runtime using the same typed-schema source as compile-time types before State entry.','UX contract types or external payload entry.','ux_contract','Runtime validation applies to HTTP/RPC/MCP/files/websocket/events/agent/worker/URL/storage/clipboard/browser payloads; compile-time types alone cannot discharge it.',perm='Schema mechanism is local choice.||Draft/sort/filter UX types are allowed but cannot shadow backend types.',deps=U+'7-assetsurface-binding-rule',ins='product_contract untrusted design')
C(U,'11-accessibility-minimum','Public Product capability UX declares semantic structure, keyboard/platform navigation for each pointer action, dynamic focus management, custom-element annotations and contrast at declared standard.','A covered UX surface is a public face of Product capability.','ux_replay','WCAG AA is recommended web default; selected local stronger obligations govern where applicable.',ob='Cite stricter project-local refinements from design when required.',perm='Internal-only debug accessibility may be exempt with design record.||Explicit recorded scoped exemptions are assessed, not guessed; recommendation does not mandate WCAG AA for every platform.',deps=U+'13-adoption-guidance',ins='accessibility design adoption')
