C(U,'13-adoption-guidance','Adoption records covered design modules, stack justification, carrier set/diagram, pre-implementation algebras, admitted typed Product bindings, membrane/Cmd mechanism, executable replay surface, applicable accessibility refinement and explicit exemptions.','Adopting UX Method for a project or selected subset of surfaces.','ux_adoption','Adoption is per project with per-surface scope; declaration precedes implementation.',ob='Declare Sub when subscriptions apply and all applicable State/Msg/Update/Cmd shapes.||Record view-shape/effect-membrane exemptions rather than infer from implementation.',perm='A project may cover production UI while excluding internal debug tools through recorded scope, subject to default/scaffold law.',deps=U+'13a-scaffold-and-exemption-law '+U+'7-assetsurface-binding-rule '+U+'8a-msg-replay-proof-requirement '+U+'11-accessibility-minimum',ins='adoption design algebras product_contract replay accessibility')
C(U,'13a-scaffold-and-exemption-law','Default UX coverage applies to shell-reachable, proof-used, Product-mutating, work-dispatching or Context/selection/closure/continuation/evidence/provenance-affecting surfaces unless a complete scoped exemption governs.','Classifying scaffold/prototype/debug/temporary proof surfaces under UX adoption and default coverage.','ux_adoption','Exempt scaffolds cannot accumulate into production UX or silently enter Product closure.',ob='Exemption record names scope, permitted operations, forbidden/bounded mutation, user-facing label, superseding authoritative surface, retirement condition/owning ticket and non-closure condition preventing release if scaffold remains.||Retire, reprice into governed UX, or keep outside closure.',perm='A valid recorded bounded exemption permits only named operations and applicability; a debug label alone is insufficient.',deps=U+'13-adoption-guidance '+U+'1a-constitutional-authority-rule',ins='adoption design product_contract')
C(U,'13b-ux-sprint-compliance-escrow','Short UX iteration may defer permitted local proof/cleanup when per-change proof costs exceed expected correction cost, but each changed item retains its compliance result and every debt/treatment must be classified before sprint-close eligibility.','A UX sprint explicitly selects compliance escrow under Spec/Ticket authority.','ux_escrow','UX controls allow/deny scope and forensic walkthrough; Ticket owns six treatment classes and sprint closure; Product UX closure still requires applicable replay/accessibility.',ob='Escrow only capture/visual review/copy-spacing-density-layout/accessibility review-remediation/replay updates/design wording/trace cleanup.||Do not escrow missing truth-changing carriers, new/changed typed Product contracts, meaning-changing navigation/IA/selection, runtime/governance/closure/continuation/lineage/provenance/evidence semantics, release criteria or method law.||Forbidden finding exits through standalone repricing or sprint supersession.||Walk every changed screen/state/interaction against authority at close; classify each finding with separate compliance and competent disposition evidence; preserve failures, uncertainty, performance and effects.||Close only with classified permitted debt and durable follow-up; unclassified carrier gaps/hidden continuation/authority drift prohibit close.||Applicable replay/accessibility proof remains owed for Product method closure; sprint close neither repays debt nor establishes closure.',perm='May close with explicit local paydown tickets only when debt is local UX realization and governing law permits follow-up.||Valid close triggers include timebox end, excessive changed states, stale walkthrough evidence, behavior beyond polish or reviewer uncertainty.||Recorded authorized exemption changes only named applicability.',deps='TICKET_METHOD.sprint-close-review|treatment_and_closure_owner '+T+'contract-application|assessment_admission '+F+'result-conjunction|closure_contract '+U+'8a-msg-replay-proof-requirement '+U+'11-accessibility-minimum',ins='sprint adoption design replay accessibility product_contract',mapping={'contract_ref':'core_result','local_predicates':{'item_compliance':'changed screen/state/interaction meets applicable UX and cited design obligations at exact basis','decision':'one of six treatments selected under actual sprint mandate','sprint_close':'all items/debts classified, follow-up durable and surviving local debt permitted','method_closure':'all applicable UX obligations including per-family replay and accessibility established'},'treatment_values':['accepted','local_paydown','design_reframe','requirement_reprice','product_reprice','remove'],'reason_sensitive':'Every raw treatment retains separately assessed compliant/failure/insufficient/invalid_basis/out_of_frame reason. Local paydown may retain failure or uncertainty; remove can be lawful without a proven defect.','non_implications':['local_paydown does not establish compliance','sprint closed does not establish repayment','replay debt deferral does not establish replay proof','authorized exemption does not validate unrelated obligations']},extra={'contract_bindings':[{'contract':'TICKET_METHOD.sprint-close-review','local_subject':'each changed screen/state/product-meaningful interaction with current scope and cited UX/design authority','item_predicate':'current applicable UX/design obligations hold','compliance_map':{'satisfied':'all applicable obligations and required acceptance established','falsified':'demonstrated unmet obligation or authority drift','indeterminate':'unproved obligation, unresolved applicability/requirement or missing reason','invalid_basis':'uninterpretable/contradictory subject or basis','out_of_frame':'outside assessment scope/capability'},'separate_decision':'treatment selected under bound mandate, preserving original assessment and effects','close_condition':'classification complete and permitted local follow-up durable; no unclassified carrier/continuation/authority gaps'}]})
